patch 346 -- thread the 5 near reloc-applier install/clear sites via the loader shim (pairs with 345).

The 5 near reloc-applier sites `xor bx,bx; mov si,<off>; lcall [ds:0x0a]` (0x1384 si=0x2c4, 0x1c78
si=0x378, 0x216d si=0x39c, 0xfa7c si=0x8c, 0x14b24 si=0x258) install DGROUP near vectors from the engine's
own reloc table (seg 0x3352:si) via FUN_0000_f7ef (DGROUP:0x0a).  Ghidra rendered f7ef inert (merged with
f81a, dropped the f7c3 retry + DS:SI walk) AND dropped the SI arg at every indirect service call, so f7ef
cannot be driven with the right section.  Until now the base-lost 11e0 zeroed DGROUP:0x0a so these lcalls
no-op-trapped; patch 345 keeps 0x0a live (= f7ef), which would fire the base-lost f7ef on garbage SI ->
SIGSEGV (the 1384 crash).  Thread each site faithfully to the loader-role shim
fist_apply_reloc_section(si,0) (near: skip the leading base word, addend=base<<4=0 in base-0), and each
matched clear site `mov si,<off>; lcall [ds:0x0e]` (f81d) to fist_clear_reloc_section(si).  4b16 (patch 022)
already had the correct fist_apply_reloc_section(0x258,0) alongside a now-live stray lcall [0x0a] -- the
stray is dropped.  The near shim path itself was fixed (it never skipped the near leading word -> was a
silent 0-entry no-op; asm-verified fix vs f7ef 0xf7fa..0xf815, f81d clear 0xf828..0xf83a) in
tools/native_main.c.  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.
